# 9. DATABASE INTEGRITY AND DELETION RULES

Implement the proper foreign keys, indexes, constraints, and deletion rules.

## General rules

- Use RESTRICT or SET NULL for historical or official records where appropriate.
- Do not cascade-delete official or historical records.
- Junction tables may use CASCADE only where it is safe.
- Never delete historical accomplishment reviews.
- Never delete accomplishment submissions.
- Never delete evidence records belonging to historical submissions.
- Never delete attendance history.
- Never delete service-hour adjustments.
- Never delete official generated reports.
- Never delete report items that are required for historical integrity.
- Never delete audit logs.
- Prefer soft deletion, archival, or deactivation where appropriate.

The database must protect historical records even if a related user, task, or academic record becomes inactive.

